{"id":"elon","name":"Elon","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:elon"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Elon","text":"Oak. (1.) A city of Dan (Josh. 19:43). (2.) A Hittite, father of Bashemath, Esau’s wife (Gen. 26:34). (3.) One of the sons of Zebulun (Gen. 46:14). (4.) The eleventh of the Hebrew judges. He held office for ten years (Judg. 12:11, 12). He is called the Zebulonite."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H356","lemma":"אֵילוֹן","xlit":"ʼÊylôwn","gloss":"Elon, the name of a place in Palestine, and also of one","kjv":"Elon","count":7,"share":1},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":3,"share":0.43}],"verses":["Gen.26.34","Gen.36.2","Gen.46.14","Num.26.26","Josh.19.43","Judg.12.11","Judg.12.12"],"related":[{"id":"zebulun-the-tribe-of","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.06,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abdon","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"accursed","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"achbor","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adaiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adrammelech","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"aharah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFXI.1","count":1,"book":"The Stromata, or Miscellanie","title":"Book I"}]},{"work":"jubilees","title":"Jubilees","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Jub.44","count":1,"book":"Jub.","title":""}]}]}
